REPLACE_ME_WITH_YOUR_REAL_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY

If you're only using the .env-based approach and don't intend to switch
to this file-based secret, you can leave this placeholder content as-is
after copying it to secrets/DEEPSEEK_API_KEY — Docker Compose still
requires the file to exist (see docker-compose.yml's SECRETS comment),
but an OS/.env-supplied DEEPSEEK_API_KEY environment variable always
takes precedence over this file's content, so a placeholder here is
harmless in that case.

To actually use this file:
  1. cp secrets/DEEPSEEK_API_KEY.example secrets/DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
  2. replace the placeholder line above with your real key (and nothing else in the file)
  3. remove/comment out DEEPSEEK_API_KEY from .env
